# _*** UPDATED - Added CSS Syntax support for selectors ***_

## Adds `inject_as`, `selector`, `root` features to `props` attribute, to enable automatic injection of properties into an `rsx!` definition.

The basic principle is to be able to declaratively inject values of a custom component onto tags or other components in the `rsx!` definition of that custom component.

### `inject_as` - maps name

* `inject_as` is an optional attribute name mapper of the value to inject, _i.e._<br>
`my_class` => `class` or <br>
`clicky` => `onclick`

### `selector` injects attribute values or event handlers:

* `selector` is a `;` separated list of pseudo `css` like selectors that indicate where to inject the value<br>

   *  `:root` - root element, only if root level has only one element
   *  `:any` - any element in level
   *  `tag | component` - _i.e., div | MyCustomComponent
   *  `:` - similar to `css` pseudo selector, marks the declaration of a child selector
   * `:first` - first child in elements list
   * `:last` - last child in elements list
   * `:even` - even children in elements list
   * `:odd` - odd children, in elements list
   * `:only` - only child, in elements list
   *  `:[nth[,nth]]` - comma delimited list of `nth` children
   *  `:last[nth[,nth]]` - comma delimited list of `nth` children from end
   *  `:[Nn±B]` - every N, _i.e._ `div:[3n]` _every 3rd element that is_ `div`
   *  `:[..nth]` - the first `nth` children
   *  `:[nth..]` - all children from `nth` onward
   *  `@` - similar to `:`, but marks the declaration child-of-type selector
   * `@first` - first child-of-type in elements list
   * `@last` - last child-of-type in elements list
   * `@even` - even children-of-type in elements list
   * `@odd` - odd children-of-type, in elements list
   * `@only` - only child of type, in elements list
   *  `@[nth[,nth]]` - comma delimited list of `nth` children-of-type
   *  `@last[nth[,nth]]` - comma delimited list of `nth` children-of-type from end
   *  `@[Nn]` - every N, _i.e._ `div:[3n]` _every 3rd_ `div`
   *  `@[..nth]` - the first `nth` children-of-type
   *  `@[nth..]` - all children-of-type from `nth` onward
   *  `>` - similar to `css` child selector
   *  `;` - is a divider for subsequent selectors, _values can be injected more than once_

###  `root` injects attribute values or event handlers only to a `root` element:

`root` is equivalent to, therefore a shortcut of `selector = ":root"`

### one addition to `rsx!` syntax

To make the automatic inject possible the `rsx!` needs to know the custom context type as well as custom context instance name. The syntax has been extended to take the form `name:type;`, _i,e., `rsx! { cx: Component; ... }`_

This requirement for injection does not preclude or interfere with the original definition of `rsx!`, it just extends it for this use case.

## Manual Example

```rust
#[derive(Props)]
pub struct ComponentProps<'a> {
    #[props(default)]
    my_class: &'a str,
    #[props(default)]
    onclick: EventHandler<'a, MouseEvent>,
    children: Element<'a>,
}

#[allow(non_snake_case)]
pub fn Component<'a>(cx: Scope<'a, ComponentProps<'a>>) -> Element {
    cx.render(rsx! {
        div {
            onclick: move |evt| cx.props.onclick.call(evt),
            a {
                "class": "{cx.props.my_class}"
            }
            &cx.props.children
        }
        div {
            onclick: move |evt| cx.props.onclick.call(evt),
            "class": "{cx.props.my_class}"
        }
    })
}

#[attributes(optional(div), exclude(class, name, id))]
#[derive(Props)]
pub struct Component2Prop<'a> {
    #[props(default)]
    class: &'a str,
    #[props(default)]
    onclick: EventHandler<'a, MouseEvent>,
    children: Element<'a>,
}

#[allow(non_snake_case)]
pub fn Component2<'a>(cx: Scope<'a, Component2Prop<'a>>) -> Element {
    cx.render(rsx! {
        div {
            Component {
                my_class: "{cx.props.class}",
                onclick: move |evt| cx.props.onclick.call(evt),
                &cx.props.children,
            }
            div {}
        }
        div {}
    })
}
```

## Declarative Equivalent

```rust
use dioxus::events::MouseEvent;
use dioxus::prelude::*;

use dioxus_sugar::attributes;

#[attributes(optional(div), exclude(class, name, id))]
#[derive(Props)]
pub struct ComponentProps<'a> {
    #[props(default, inject_as = "class", selector= "div:[1]; div:first > a")]
    my_class: &'a str,
    #[props(default, selector= "div")]
    onclick: EventHandler<'a, MouseEvent>,
    children: Element<'a>,
}

#[allow(non_snake_case)]
pub fn Component<'a>(cx: Scope<'a, ComponentProps<'a>>) -> Element {
    rsx! {
        cx: ComponentProps;
        div {
            a {}
            &cx.props.children
        }
        div {}
    }
}

#[derive(Props)]
pub struct Component2Prop<'a> {
    #[props(default, inject_as = "my_class", selector = "div > Component")]
    class: &'a str,
    #[props(default, selector = "div > Component")]
    onclick: EventHandler<'a, MouseEvent>,
    children: Element<'a>,
}

#[allow(non_snake_case)]
pub fn Component2<'a>(cx: Scope<'a, Component2Prop<'a>>) -> Element {
    rsx! {
        cx: Component2Prop;
        div {
            Component {
                &cx.props.children,
            }
            div {}
        }
        div {}
    }
}
```

## Motivation

The idea was born out of supporting [Dioxus-Sugar](https://github.com/Nejat/dioxus-sugar) which declaratively includes valid html attributes and event handlers for custom component properties. `Dioxus-Sugar` adds the attribute and event handler definitions to the custom component properties and this feature injects those and other custom properties into the custom component definition. Which lets me finish my ultimate reason for building any of these `Dioxus-Bulma` :)

## Supports CSS Selector and a more concise "rusty" equivalent

this is a list of supported selectors, the left side is the new css syntax and the right side is the original more concise "rusty" syntax

```
:not(p)						:not[p] 

element:nth-child(n)				element:[n]

element:nth-child(an ± b)			element:[an ± b]

element:nth-child(even)				element:even

element:nth-child(odd)				element:odd

element:nth-last-child(n)			element:last[n]

element:first-child				element:first

element:last-child				element:last

element:only-child				element:only


element:nth-of-type(n)				element@[n]

element:nth-of-type(an ± b)			element@[an ± b]

element:nth-of-type(even)			element@even

element:nth-of-type(odd)			element@odd

element:nth-last-of-type(n)			element@last[n]

element:first-of-type				element@first

element:last-of-type				element@last

element:only-of-type				element@only


PLUS Non-CSS

:root

:any						*


element:nth-child(n1..n2)			element:[n1..n2]

element:nth-child(..n)				element:[..n]

element:nth-child(n..)				element:[n..]


element:nth-of-type(n1..n2)			element@[n1..n2]

element:nth-of-type(..n)			element@[..n]

element:nth-of-type(n..)			element@[n..]
```

